The image illustrates the physical characteristics of Nano-11 nanoparticles, a plant-derived vaccine adjuvant. The Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image shows spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like surface, indicating their dendrimer-like structure. Dynamic light scattering (DLS) data further reveals a uniform size distribution, with the majority of particles falling between 30 and 110 nm, and a Z-average hydrodynamic diameter consistently around 70-80 nm, a size range conducive to efficient uptake by dendritic cells.